{:paths ["src" "resources"]

 ;; NIST v2-validation engine (profile-tier HL7 v2 judge). These
 ;; coordinates do NOT resolve from Maven Central. They resolve from
 ;; CDC's public lib-hl7v2-nist-validator repository, its Maven-layout
 ;; lib/ tree pinned by commit -- add to the ROOT deps.edn (:mvn/repos
 ;; is only honored at the root):
 ;;
 ;;   :mvn/repos {"nist-hit" {:url "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CDCgov/lib-hl7v2-nist-validator/eeac90c5f88dca3018992005232acdf3da644d88/lib/"}}
 ;;
 ;; Until 2026-11-17 that URL was NIST's own Nexus,
 ;; https://hit-nexus.nist.gov/repository/releases/. On that date the
 ;; host was observed answering 302 to a web page, Maven received HTML
 ;; for the jars, and the author ruled CDC's repository an accepted
 ;; channel for these six coordinates, superseding for them the
 ;; NIST-channel clause of the amendment cited below
 ;; (.agents/session-records/2026-11-17-nist-channel-cdc-pin.md). The
 ;; pin is a commit, so the URL cannot change under a build; the
 ;; content authority is still the lock's sha256, not the host.
 ;;
 ;; Determinism note (artifacts.lock.edn discipline; ADR-0053, AR-F4-4):
 ;; jar sha256s are recorded in the root artifacts.lock.edn. Vendoring
 ;; these jars into an IN-REPO file:// mirror is FORECLOSED (ADR-0005's
 ;; 2026-07-24 amendment, notes/tools/ADRs.md): these coordinates are
 ;; license-unstated at the coordinate level -- this repo
 ;; redistributes none of them. The safe end-state instead is a
 ;; USER-SIDE mirror, outside this repo: `bin/mirror-nist` / `make
 ;; mirror-nist` builds ~/.ehrt/nist-mirror/ from the invoking user's
 ;; own already-fetched ~/.m2 cache, sha256-verified against
 ;; artifacts.lock.edn; `bin/verify-nist-lock` / `make verify-nist-lock`
 ;; (wired into `make test`) checks the lockfile's own claims against
 ;; ~/.m2 on every per-push run. See
 ;; components/judge-v2-nist/docs/nist-mirror.md. (CDC's own
 ;; gov.cdc:lib-hl7v2-nist-validator vendors these same six jars into an
 ;; IN-REPO file:// mirror -- a legitimate design for a build CDC itself
 ;; controls and redistributes; not available to this repo under the
 ;; amendment above. It is that tree the URL above reads, over the
 ;; network; no jar of it enters this repo.)
 ;;
 ;; Transitive deps beyond these three (scala-library 2.13.10, typesafe
 ;; config 1.4.2, commons-lang3, xom 1.3.7, scala-xml_2.13 1.3.0,
 ;; jackson, httpclient 4.5.9) DO resolve from Maven Central normally.
 :deps {gov.nist/hl7-v2-validation {:mvn/version "1.7.3"}
        gov.nist/hl7-v2-parser     {:mvn/version "1.7.3"}
        gov.nist/hl7-v2-profile    {:mvn/version "1.7.3"}}

 :aliases {:test {:extra-paths ["test"]
                  :extra-deps {org.clojure/test.check {:mvn/version "1.1.3"}
                               org.slf4j/slf4j-nop {:mvn/version "2.0.17"}}}}}
